{{Use dmy dates|date=November 2022}}
{{Use British English|date=November 2025}}
The '''Waterstones Book of the Year''', established in 2012,<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |last=Cain |first=Sian |date=2018-11-29 |title=Sally Rooney's Normal People named Waterstones book of the year |url=http://www.theguardian.com/books/2018/nov/29/sally-rooneys-normal-people-named-waterstones-book-of-the-year |access-date=2022-07-23 |website=the Guardian |language=en |archive-date=30 June 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220630073030/https://www.theguardian.com/books/2018/nov/29/sally-rooneys-normal-people-named-waterstones-book-of-the-year |url-status=live }}</ref> is an annual award presented to a book published in the previous 12 months. [[Waterstones]]' booksellers nominate and vote to determine the winners and finalists for the prize.

Award winners receive "full and committed backing" from Waterstones both in-person and online.<ref name=":2">{{Cite web |last= |first= |date=2018-11-08 |title=Awards: Waterstones, Blackwell's Books of the Year Finalists |url=https://www.shelf-awareness.com/issue.html?issue=3372 |access-date=2022-07-23 |website=Shelf Awareness |archive-date=23 July 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220723234950/https://www.shelf-awareness.com/issue.html?issue=3372 |url-status=live }}</ref>

